Why: metislib.h includes libmetis' own headers with <...>, which needs
 libmetis on the include path of every C file in the package; its generic
 names (defs.h, macros.h, proto.h, struct.h) would then shadow PORD's
 macros.h and any system header of the same name. Quoted includes are
 found next to metislib.h.
Upstream: not sent (METIS 5.1.0 is no longer maintained in this form).
Obsolete when: METIS is replaced.

